description:
The map of emem's tools, and the one tool that finds all the others. It gives the working loop in order (name, ground, cite, resolve, verify, check for drift). Then it groups every other tool by the question it answers, each with a one-line trigger. Send `name` for the full schema of one tool and an example that runs. IF YOU SEE A LIST OF 18 TOOLS, IT IS A CURATED SUBSET OF 115, NOT THE FULL SURFACE. Hosts remove `_meta`, so this text repeats the count. You can call every catalogued tool by name through tools/call at either endpoint.

When to use: Call this FIRST when you do not know which tool answers the question. Also call it when your list does not have a capability. A tool that is not in your list can still be on the server. `q` searches by topic (`ndvi`, `flood`, `verify`). `name` returns one exact schema. With no arguments, you get the full map. /mcp/full registers the full catalog. emem_ask answers in one call without a choice of primitive.

Example arguments: {"q":"ndvi"}
